{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Why did Sarah laugh.</b> And if you ask: why did HaShem not take Abraham to task as He took Sarah to task, for Abraham too laughed just as much, as stated in the last passage of the portion of Lekh Lekha? One may answer: it is like a wise woman who came to reprove her daughter-in-law but reproved her own daughter, and her daughter-in-law understood on her own. So too, had HaShem reprove Abraham to his face, Abraham would have been ashamed; instead He reproved him from the side." "<b>And I have grown old.</b> Rashi: Scripture altered for the sake of peace, that is to say, this is what Sarah said: is it possible for me to have a remedy for bearing a child? For 'after I have grown worn' means 'I have grown old'; I knew that I had youthfulness and vigor, for I had my menstrual flow; and 'my master is old' — that is to say, all this is of no avail to me, for my master is old, and how shall I conceive again? If so, she attributed the old age entirely to Abraham, and in this Scripture altered."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:43.438379784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}